Package: fmriAR
Type: Package
Title: Fast Autoregressive (AR) and ARMA Prewhitening for Functional MRI (fMRI)
    Design and Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Bradley", "Buchsbaum", email = "brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com", role = c("aut","cre"))
Author: Bradley Buchsbaum [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Bradley Buchsbaum <brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com>
Description: Lightweight utilities to estimate autoregressive (AR) and
    autoregressive moving average (ARMA) noise models from residuals and apply
    matched generalized least squares (GLS) prewhitening to functional magnetic
    resonance imaging (fMRI) design and data matrices. The ARMA estimator
    follows Hannan and Rissanen (1982) <doi:10.1093/biomet/69.1.81>, and the
    Analysis of Functional NeuroImages (AFNI)-inspired restricted AR family
    mirrors the workflow described by Cox (2012)
    <doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2011.08.056>.
